Catalogue a file whose tag holds an item lofty cannot parse.

Why: lofty's default mode fails the whole file on one bad item. 5 MP3s in the
library carry a TDRL (release time) frame holding a web address instead of a
date; every scan skipped them as TAG_READ_FAILED, so they were missing from
the catalogue (checked 2026-10-24 against lofty 0.25.4: BestAttempt fails,
Relaxed reads 29-36 items each). The catalogue reads (scan metadata, tag
half, cover art) now use lofty's Relaxed mode, which drops the bad item. The
save path keeps the default mode, so such a file is still refused for writes
and left as it is.

Not covered: a frame whose size is corrupt (one file here, a COMM frame) still
fails in Relaxed mode too.

Tests: new test with a TDRL holding a web address reads, and a save is
refused with the file unchanged; it fails without the fix.

Remove when: upstream reads leniently or lofty skips such items by default.

